#: modules/univention/admin/handlers/shares/share.py:298
msgid "Oplocks are the way that Samba clients get permission from a server to locally cache file operations.  If a server grants an oplock (opportunistic lock) then the client is free to assume that it is the only one accessing the file and it will aggressively cache file data. With some  oplock  types the client may even cache file open/close operations. This can give enormous performance benefits. When you activate this parameter, Samba will always grant oplock requests no matter how many clients are using the file. It is generally much better to use the real oplocks support rather than this parameter. If you enable this option on all read-only shares or shares that you know will only be accessed from one client at a time such as physically read-only media like CDROMs, you will see a big performance improvement on many operations. If you enable this option on shares where multiple clients may be accessing the files read-write at the same  time you can get data corruption. Use this option carefully!"
msgstr "Oplocks 是 Samba 用戶端從伺服器取得在本機快取檔案操作之權限的方式。若伺服器授予 oplock (opportunistic lock)，則用戶端可自由假設只有它在存取該檔案，並會積極地快取檔案資料。在某些 oplock 類型下，用戶端甚至可快取檔案開啟/關閉操作。這可帶來巨大的效能優勢。當您啟用此參數時，無論有多少用戶端正在使用該檔案，Samba 都會一律授予 oplock 要求。一般而言，使用真正的 oplocks 支援會比此參數好得多。若您在所有唯讀共用，或您確知一次只會由一個用戶端存取的共用 (例如 CDROM 等實體唯讀媒體) 上啟用此選項，您將在許多操作上看到顯著的效能改善。若您在可能有多個用戶端同時讀寫存取檔案的共用上啟用此選項，可能會導致資料損毀。請謹慎使用此選項！"

